    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0045" n="35" xml:id="pg35"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Earl
                        Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 5, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> I have the honor to transmit copies of
                    several depositions fur nished to me by Mr. Underwood, the consul of the United
                    States at Glasgow, all relating to the outfit of the vessel called the Canton or
                    the Pampero at that port.</p>
                <p>I pray your lordship to accept the assurances of the highest consideration with
                    which I have the honor to be, my lord, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell, &amp;</hi><hi
                            rendition="#italic">c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
